[#:seon.task{:name "task-creation-is-not-an-agent-call"
             :plan "my.task (the agent-facing API) exposes `my.task/current` and `my.task/send-back!` but not task creation or refinement: `seon.task/create!` upserts a runtime task from a declaration, yet (dir my.task) does not list a call over it, so an agent cannot file a finding as a task or edit its own task. Done when `my.task/update!` over `seon.task/create!`'s upsert, with the agent's world supplied, is listed by (dir my.task), documented with an example, and a regression edits a task from an agent's evaluation (plan §0 item 6)."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-send-back-stores-its-counterexample-for-the-next-attempts-agent"
             :plan "`my.task/send-back!` accepts `:my.task/counterexample` and returns it in its reply, but no attribute stores it: `seon.turn/end-task-call` writes the reason and target on the sending attempt, and `seon.context/send-backs` (the `:seon.context/send-backs` block of `my.task/current` and the current-state block) renders only the reason, so the next attempt's agent never sees the counterexample (step-context lane). Declare the counterexample as a Malli-schemed attribute on the sending attempt, written by `seon.turn/end-task-call` in the same transaction as the reason, and have `seon.context/send-backs` carry it as data beside the reason. Proof: the `my.task-test` deftest `a-send-back-with-a-counterexample-shows-it-to-the-next-attempt` the implementer writes first sends back with `{:expected 1 :actual 2}`, launches the target's next attempt and asserts `(:seon.context/send-backs (my.task/current))` holds that map."}
 #:seon.task{:name "reading-the-current-task-mid-attempt-costs-gigabytes"
             :plan "Live run 13 (`docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-19/live-run-13.md`), Design and Prove attempts on default at 4313acf79: single forms reading `my.task/current` cost 1.4 to 4.3 s and 1.8 to 3.7 GB, against 69 ms and 90 MB for the same read at the attempt's start. Forms (attempt, form): a Design's `my.task/update!` of its own plan, `(get-in (my.task/current) [:seon.context/task :seon.task/sym])` as the task, 4,266 ms 3,682 MB (c9faebbf6e29, 24); `(def next-task (get-in (my.task/current) [:seon.context/chain :seon.context/after 0 :seon.task/sym]))` 1,618 ms 2,276 MB (4bec20fc6ff4, 28); the Prove template's own `my.task/update!` of the next task's proofs 1,445 ms 1,845 MB (4bec20fc6ff4, 31); a `let` pulling the current task and its next one 1,768 ms 2,623 MB (fc99cdd864e6, 48). Each came after the agent had defined a deftest or run a check on its branch. Measure one of them with `seon.profile/measure` on a kept branch (`:chain-16572b11dd32`, `:chain-6097a5caea6f`), name the instrumented functions responsible, and fix that producer; related: `seon.context/one-agents-current-state-costs-hundreds-of-megabytes`. Measured by lane run13-fixes (2026-10-19, default b88d9365d, JVM mode, `seon.profile/measure`): the cost is `seon.context/step-verdict` (the done rule's input, `seon.context/judged-input`) computed cold for new branch content, not the read of the task. Cold on `:chain-16572b11dd32` (history, a new deftest on the branch): `step-verdict` 2,358 ms, 913 MB on the calling thread (2.3 GB request-wide), the whole `seon.context/task-sections` after it 328 ms; warm 12 ms. Split on the cold `:chain-cd8a339333ef` (6 changed declarations, 20 judged members): `seon.cluster.source/merge-members` 266 ms 166 MB, `seon.context/current-results` of the members 663 ms 265 MB (`seon.test.runner/reach-index`, `reach-fixed-point`, `reach-component-digests`: the whole program's reach graph per change, `seon.test.runner/tests-reaching-rebuilds-the-whole-program-reach-graph-per-change`), `seon.cluster.source/publication` 800 ms 542 MB (its `seon.cluster.source/file-proof`: `seon.fn.analyzer/invoke-kondo` lints every changed file whole, 361 ms self for 4 calls, plus clj-kondo's own threads). Main moving alone costs 104 to 282 ms (publication keyed by main's commit; the file proof is reused). What grows with the attempt is the branch's changed declarations and files: each new content pays the file proof and the reach graph again, whichever request reads the verdict first. Fix at those owners (file proof proportional to the changed forms, reach index incremental), both in `src/seon/cluster/source.clj` and `src/seon/test/runner.clj`; then add a `seon.cost-estimate-test` row for `my.task/current` after one new deftest."}
